---
Scope per manifest: internal/services/metrics/metrics.go (+2 test files, one kept unmodified
from attempt 1, one new), internal/handlers/dashboard/handlers.go (+3 test files, 2 kept + 1
new wiring test), internal/services/mcpsvc/spend/{register,summary}.go (transitively fixed,
+test), plus the sanctioned mechanical edits. Confirmed via `git status --porcelain` and
`git diff` hunk reads.

FIRST: re-ran attempt 1's winning probe through the real, fixed Calculate(). Confirmed the
CONCEDED counterexample is now correct: $2,000 payment + $2,500 refund flagged group beside
$3,000 rent now produces LivingExpensesTotal=3000, PlanExcludedTotal=-500 (signed, negative =
net refund) — exactly per ruling SY-2026-08-30c. Attempt 1's specific defect is genuinely
fixed.

ATTACK 1 — Sign consistency between the four fixed sites. Read all four diff hunks
(metrics.go range total, per-month trend, combined walk; handlers.go per-month Living bar):
all four use the identical `-pe.SumAmount()`/`-planExcludedSet.SumAmount()` convention, no
site left on math.Abs (confirmed via the manifest's own `grep -rn "math.Abs"` output, which I
independently re-ran: math.Abs remains only on totalExpenses/healthcareTotal/expAmt/hcAmt, none
on any planExcluded* value). No inter-site sign inconsistency found for the combination the
new tests exercise.

ATTACK 2 — Combined cumulative walk reconciliation with a sign-flipping flagged group mid-range.
Read TestCalculateMetrics_PlanExclusions_NetRefundCombinedCumulativeBalanceInvariantHolds: it
re-verifies `last == -CombinedCumulativeDelta` with a Jan net-refund flagged group beside a
flat Feb, and PASSES for real (re-ran it). The walk's independent signed-net subtraction stays
